{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-328234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-328234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{7}{4}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-328234" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01da23f653e5f65150b5911aeab7a13a958c3bb55c1d6e7287af659b69cfd5da"} {"question" "q-328234" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file"