stion-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-328234" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-78247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}72 \\\\ -40\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-78247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}72 \\\\ -40\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=8v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=8.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-78247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/activity-m