b7c285"} {"question" "q-328216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=2v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=2.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-328216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01da23f653e5f65150b5911aeab7a13a958c3bb55c1d6e7287af659b69cfd5da"} {"question" "q-328216" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-328216" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cf74403585a2158aafb51f1ab8af2700f117e59e984fd0ad6fda4b3ab7c285"} {"question" "q-328216" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy